# ==============================================================================
# Bible Engine Environment Variables Template (.env.example)
# ==============================================================================
# Copy this template to .env for local configuration:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is strictly ignored by git and will NEVER be uploaded to GitHub.
# API keys are also automatically discovered from config/esv_api_key.txt,
# config/gemini_api_key.txt, or ~/.config/bible/.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Crossway ESV API Key (Application Development & Scripture Ingestion)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free developer key available at: https://api.esv.org/
# Used by developers and autonomous agents for:
#   - Live ESV passage queries and side-by-side translation comparisons
#   - Scripture context retrieval during application development
#   - Semantic tagging and embedding generation
# Note: Stored locally in .env or config/esv_api_key.txt with POSIX 0600 permissions.
ESV_API_KEY=your_esv_api_key_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Google Gemini API Key (Runtime App Serving ONLY)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Free developer key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/
# SCOPE NOTICE:
#   - Needed ONLY for serving the app (interactive Scripture RAG synthesis
#     and Biblical Character Dialogue in './bible serve' or './bible chat').
#   - NOT needed for application development tasks (such as semantic tagging,
#     theological review, or code analysis). Autonomous agents developing
#     the app ARE Gemini and use local skills (skills/semantic-tagging/)
#     directly without making redundant external API calls.
#   - Prompted interactively during './bible init' or './bible keys wizard'.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
